e}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/pulls/8162","html_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/8162","diff_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/8162.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/8162.patch","merged_at":"2014-10-22T08:37:48Z"},"body":"Previously, the leniency was on a per-query basis, with each query being\nparsed into multiple queries, one for each field. If any one of these\nqueries failed, the entire query was discarded in the name of being\nlenient.\n\nNow query parts will only be discarded if they fail for a particular\nfield, the entire query is not discarded. This helps when performing a\nquery over a numeric and string field, as only the sub-queries that are\ninvalid due to format exceptions will be discarded.\n\nAlso moves the `simple_query_string` queries out of SimpleQueryTests and\ninto a dedicated SimpleQueryStringTests class.\n\nFixes #7967\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/8162/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/8162/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":181989916,"node_id":"MDE1OlJlZmVyZW5jZWRFdmVudDE4MTk4OTkxNg==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/events/181989916","actor":{"login":"dakrone","id":19060,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MDYw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19060?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dakrone","html_url":"https://github.com/dakrone","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dakrone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dakrone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dakrone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dakrone/starred{/owner}{/re